---
deadlock_detection: false
---

# The token that guards serve's /api, and answers the page does not
# expect.
#
# serve.Guard (internal/serve/auth.go) lets an /api request through only
# with the per-install token (serveclient.LoadToken, ~/.bough/serve.token)
# as a Bearer header or as the bough_serve_token cookie, which GET / sets
# for a loopback Host or the one --host name a proxy forwards. An unknown
# Host is refused 403 before anything, the page included; a non-loopback
# bind (--insecure) drops the Host check but never sets the cookie. The
# page (web/src) reads the API through api.ts req(), useCatalogue
# (app.tsx) and one EventSource per open session (api.ts subscribe).
# Children (plugins/workers) call serve with a Bearer that
# serveclient.Addr re-reads from the token file on every call.
#
# This spec is the behaviour serve and the page OWE, not the code as it
# stands. Each constant below names a design choice the claims depend
# on; flipping it to False is the code as the spec found it (REFRESH
# already held; PORT_SCOPED and WAIT_TOKEN hold since the server walk,
# mbt/serve_auth_answers_test.go), and is also the mutation that shows the claim
# guarding it can fail:
#
#   PORT_SCOPED  the cookie a tab sends is set only by its own serve.
#                Today the name is one global "bough_serve_token", and a
#                browser does not scope cookies by port: loading a second
#                serve's page on the same host (a fixture-HOME preview on
#                another port) overwrites the first serve's cookie and
#                every /api call of the first tab then answers 401; a
#                Reload of the first breaks the second the same way.
#                Now the cookie is named for serve's port (CookieName).
#   REAUTH_401   a 401 is shown as "reload to re-authorize". Today the
#                list shows the raw "serve: missing or wrong token" as if
#                it were any other failure.
#   STREAM_401   an event stream refused 401 says so. Today EventSource
#                gives up on a non-stream answer and subscribe() has no
#                onerror: the transcript silently stops updating.
#   CHECK_OK     every fetch checks res.ok before using the body as data.
#                Today useCatalogue stores a 401/5xx {"error"} body as
#                the catalogue and Controls' cat?.providers.flatMap
#                throws in render. (An HTML 502 is caught: r.json()
#                throws. ContextPage reads c.providers?. and is safe.)
#   WAIT_TOKEN   a LoadToken inside another's O_EXCL-create-then-write
#                window returns the creator's token. Today it fails
#                "serveclient: token file ... is empty". Now it waits.
#   REFRESH      a child re-reads the token file on every call. True
#                today, so the suspected "a child's cached token is never
#                refreshed" does not hold; False shows why it matters.
#
# Tokens are abstract and relative to the running serve A:
#   fresh  the token serve A holds now
#   stale  a token of serve A before a restart that minted a new one
#   other  serve B's token (another serve on another port)
#   none   nothing
#
# Fields:
#   via      how tab A reached serve A: none (not loaded) | loopback |
#            proxy (the --host name, tailscale serve) | unknown (a Host
#            serve does not answer to) | remote (a non-loopback bind)
#   proxy    the reverse proxy in front of serve (via proxy): up | down
#            | back. It drops at most once: a proxy that is up exactly
#            while serve is down, forever, starves any recovery.
#   serve    up | starting (restarted with no token file: LoadToken is
#            creating it and serve is not listening yet)
#   disk     the token file: ok | missing | empty (created, not written)
#   jar_a    the cookie tab A sends to serve A
#   other    a tab on serve B, same host, another port, is loaded
#   jar_b    the cookie that tab sends to serve B
#   got      the last /api answer tab A read: "" | ok | 401 | 403 |
#            net (connection refused) | html502 (the proxy's own page)
#   shown    what tab A says: blank | ok | reauth ("reload to
#            re-authorize") | down (serve unreachable) | refused (the
#            Host 403 body) | crash (render threw)
#   stream   tab A's open session's EventSource: none | open | dropped
#            (serve went away; EventSource retries) | closed (refused)
#   cat      the model picker's catalogue: none | ok | failed
#   child    a running child session's Bearer: fresh (serve's token) |
#            stale (an older one, not used since a rotation) |
#            refused_intact (its last call was 401 although the token
#            file was there to read)
#   loader   a second LoadToken (another serve starting, a CLI) inside
#            the create-then-write window: none | waiting (for the
#            write; it returns that token when it lands) | error
#
# Corrections to the mapped model, from the code:
# - "ClientCachedStale" is only reachable when the token file is gone
#   and serve holds a token nobody can read (see child); Addr refreshes
#   the cache on every call otherwise.
# - OpenContext is not a separate answer: ContextPage uses optional
#   chaining and never throws; the model picker is the fetch that does.
# - The catalogue read is one step (open + answer): nothing the page
#   shows moves while it is out.

PORT_SCOPED = True
REAUTH_401 = True
STREAM_401 = True
CHECK_OK = True
WAIT_TOKEN = True
REFRESH = True

# Vias whose GET / hands the page a cookie: a Reload re-authorizes.
REAUTHORIZABLE = ["loopback", "proxy"]
# Vias on which the app itself is on screen (unknown gets the 403 body).
APP = ["loopback", "proxy", "remote"]

# What an /api request from tab A gets back right now.
def answer(r):
    if r.via == "proxy" and r.proxy == "down":
        return "net"
    if r.serve != "up":
        # tailscale serve answers its own HTML 502 for a backend that is
        # not listening; a direct request is refused.
        if r.via == "proxy":
            return "html502"
        return "net"
    # Guard refuses a Host it does not answer to, but only a serve that
    # is listening can refuse anything.
    if r.via == "unknown":
        return "403"
    if r.jar_a != "fresh":
        return "401"
    return "ok"

def page_for(a):
    if a == "ok":
        return "ok"
    if a == "401":
        if REAUTH_401:
            return "reauth"
        return "down"
    if a == "403":
        return "refused"
    return "down"

role Room:
    action Init:
        self.via = "none"
        self.proxy = "up"
        self.serve = "up"
        self.disk = "ok"
        self.jar_a = "none"
        self.other = False
        self.jar_b = "none"
        self.got = ""
        self.shown = "blank"
        self.stream = "none"
        self.cat = "none"
        # A child session already running under serve, holding the token
        # it read at its first call.
        self.child = "fresh"
        self.loader = "none"

    # GET / on via v, then the page's first list read. The cookie comes
    # only from a loopback or --host request that reached serve: a load
    # while serve is not listening (or the proxy is down) gets the
    # proxy's page or nothing, and no cookie.
    atomic func load(v):
        self.via = v
        reached = self.serve == "up" and (v != "proxy" or self.proxy != "down")
        if v in REAUTHORIZABLE and reached:
            self.jar_a = "fresh"
            if not PORT_SCOPED and self.other:
                self.jar_b = "other"
        self.stream = "none"
        self.cat = "none"
        self.got = answer(self)
        self.shown = page_for(self.got)

    atomic action LoadShellLoopback:
        require self.via == "none"
        self.load("loopback")

    atomic action LoadShellProxy:
        require self.via == "none"
        self.load("proxy")

    atomic action LoadShellUnknownHost:
        require self.via == "none"
        self.load("unknown")

    atomic action LoadShellRemote:
        require self.via == "none"
        self.load("remote")

    # The person reloads tab A. Strongly fair: a page that says "reload"
    # is eventually reloaded, even across restarts that disable it for a
    # moment again and again.
    atomic fair<strong> action Reload:
        require self.via != "none" and self.serve == "up"
        require self.via != "proxy" or self.proxy != "down"
        self.load(self.via)

    # The list poll (4 s timer): GET /api/sessions.
    atomic fair<strong> action ListPoll:
        require self.via in APP
        self.got = answer(self)
        self.shown = page_for(self.got)

    # Opening a session: EventSource /api/sessions/{id}/events.
    atomic action Subscribe:
        require self.shown == "ok" and self.stream == "none"
        a = answer(self)
        if a == "ok":
            self.got = a
            self.stream = "open"
        elif a == "401":
            self.stream = "closed"
            if STREAM_401:
                self.got = a
                self.shown = page_for(a)
        else:
            self.got = a
            self.shown = page_for(a)

    # EventSource reconnects by itself once serve listens again.
    atomic fair<strong> action StreamReconnect:
        require self.stream == "dropped" and self.serve == "up"
        require self.via != "proxy" or self.proxy != "down"
        a = answer(self)
        if a == "ok":
            self.stream = "open"
        elif a == "401":
            self.stream = "closed"
            # Today the page never reads this answer: no onerror.
            if STREAM_401:
                self.got = a
                self.shown = page_for(a)

    # Opening the model picker: useCatalogue reads GET /api/models, and
    # the answer is whatever /api answers now.
    atomic action OpenModelPicker:
        require self.shown == "ok" and self.cat != "ok"
        a = answer(self)
        self.catalogue(a)

    # The same read when serve's /api/models itself fails: 500 {"error"}.
    atomic action OpenModelPicker5xx:
        require self.shown == "ok" and self.cat != "ok"
        require answer(self) == "ok"
        self.catalogue("5xx")

    atomic func catalogue(a):
        if a == "ok":
            self.cat = "ok"
            return
        if a != "5xx":
            self.got = a
        if a in ["net", "html502"] or CHECK_OK:
            self.cat = "failed"
            if a != "5xx":
                self.shown = page_for(a)
        else:
            # A JSON {"error"} body stored as the catalogue.
            self.shown = "crash"

    # A preview serve on another port of the same host, with its own
    # fixture HOME and token, opened in another tab.
    atomic action OpenOtherServe:
        require self.via == "loopback" and not self.other
        self.other = True
        self.jar_b = "fresh"
        if not PORT_SCOPED:
            self.jar_a = "other"

    atomic action DeleteTokenFile:
        require self.disk == "ok"
        self.disk = "missing"

    # bough serve restarts; its open streams end. With the token file in
    # place it keeps the token; without one LoadToken creates the file
    # (O_EXCL) and writes a new token before serve listens.
    atomic action ServeRestart:
        require self.serve == "up"
        if self.stream == "open":
            self.stream = "dropped"
        if self.disk == "missing":
            self.disk = "empty"
            self.serve = "starting"

    atomic fair<strong> action TokenWritten:
        require self.disk == "empty"
        self.disk = "ok"
        self.serve = "up"
        if self.jar_a == "fresh":
            self.jar_a = "stale"
        if self.child == "fresh":
            self.child = "stale"
        if self.loader == "waiting":
            self.loader = "none"

    # A second LoadToken inside the create-then-write window. Owed: it
    # waits for the write and returns that token. The wait is a state
    # of its own: an action that changed nothing would be no link in
    # the graph, and no walk would ever race a LoadToken.
    atomic action ConcurrentLoadToken:
        require self.disk == "empty" and self.loader == "none"
        if WAIT_TOKEN:
            self.loader = "waiting"
        else:
            self.loader = "error"

    # A child session calls serve (tools.spawn background) with the
    # Bearer serveclient holds; Addr re-reads the token file first. Only
    # with the file in place: without it Addr keeps the Bearer it had,
    # which is the running serve's own token unless serve rotated since
    # the child's last call (see the flow notes).
    atomic action ChildCall:
        require self.serve == "up" and self.disk == "ok"
        if REFRESH:
            self.child = "fresh"
        elif self.child != "fresh":
            self.child = "refused_intact"

    atomic action ProxyDown:
        require self.via == "proxy" and self.proxy == "up"
        self.proxy = "down"

    atomic fair<strong> action ProxyUp:
        require self.via == "proxy" and self.proxy == "down"
        self.proxy = "back"

action Init:
    room = Room()

# A cookie a tab sends to its serve was set by that serve: opening a
# second serve never silently breaks the first tab, nor reloading the
# first the second.
always assertion NoForeignCookie:
    return room.jar_a != "other" and room.jar_b != "other"

# A 401 is "reload to re-authorize", never an outage or a crash.
always assertion Unauthorized401IsReauth:
    return room.got != "401" or room.shown == "reauth"

# "Serve is unreachable" is said only for an answer that did not come
# from serve's API: refused, or the proxy's own page.
always assertion DownOnlyWhenUnreachable:
    return room.shown != "down" or room.got in ["net", "html502"]

# A refused stream is on screen, never a transcript that silently stops
# under a page that still says all is well. (A later poll may say the
# proxy is down instead: that is on screen too.)
always assertion ClosedStreamSaysSo:
    return room.stream != "closed" or room.shown != "ok"

# A wrong-shaped answer never throws in render.
always assertion NeverCrashes:
    return room.shown != "crash"

# A LoadToken racing the creator returns the one token on disk.
always assertion ConcurrentLoadGetsTheToken:
    return room.loader != "error"

# A child with the token file to read is never refused.
always assertion ChildAuthWhenFileIntact:
    return room.child != "refused_intact"

# hasToken: no cookie is no token (Guard refuses an empty one), so a
# page that was never handed a cookie (a remote bind) never reads data.
always assertion NoCookieNoApi:
    return room.jar_a != "none" or room.got != "ok"

# From a reauth, a clobbered cookie, a restart onto a new token or a
# proxy outage, the tab comes back to ok, as long as it reached serve
# on a name that hands it a cookie.
always eventually assertion PageRecovers:
    return room.via not in REAUTHORIZABLE or room.shown == "ok"
